    None
} else {
    let jstr = JString::from(mime);
    let text = env.get_string(&jstr)?.to_string_lossy().into_owned();
    Some(text)
};
```

Hmm, but the error is about the temporary `JavaStr` being dropped while still borrowed — the issue is `Some(env.get_string(&jstr)?.to_string_lossy().into_owned())` — the `?` early-returns a Result, and the `JavaStr` temp... Let me just follow the suggestion exactly:

```rust
