```

Hmm, that's the same expression assigned to x. The trick is that the temporary is dropped at the end of the let statement instead of end of block. Let me apply that. Actually simpler: use `let x = ...; Some(x)`? The `?` makes it tricky. Let me write:

```rust
let mime = if mime.is_null() {
    None
} else {
    let jstr = JString::from(mime);
    let text = env.get_string(&jstr)?.to_string_lossy().into_owned();
