Confirmed: `KalFilePicker` IS in the APK (classes3.dex / classes4.dex), but the background thread's `FindClass` uses the system class loader and can't see it. This is the classic Android JNI pitfall: **`FindClass` from a thread that was attached via `AttachCurrentThread` (not created by Java) uses the system class loader, which only knows framework classes — not app classes.**

The fix: resolve `KalFilePicker` through the Activity's class loader. Plan:

1. In `pick_image_sync()` (android_picker.rs), replace `env.find_class("com/kal/calendar/KalFilePicker")` with a class-loader-based lookup:
